  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>Alex. J. Barbour is listed at No. 193 <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> in 1925 and 1930, as a stone mason in 1930. It is the first listing after the <ref target="civic?id=Little%20Pelham%20Street">Little Pelham Street</ref> corner.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>Alexander James Barbour, mason, is on the 1928 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 193 Bouverie Street.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>The fire station is next door. Before him, the hairdresser <ref target="civic?id=Robert%20William%20Hewat">Robert William Hewat</ref> was at No. 193 in 1915 and 1920.</p>
      </div>
